  "about.title": "About Octar Lab",
  "about.mission_title": "Our Mission",
  "about.mission_body": "Octar Lab exists to put serious AI-assisted tooling within arm's reach of every developer — without paywalls, without telemetry, without fine print. We believe powerful tools should be transparent, customisable, and free for everyone to use, fork, and improve. The five biggest AI providers under one roof, your keys in your own keyring, your code on your own disk. That's it. That's the whole pitch.",
  "about.octarinox_title": "About Octarinox",
  "about.octarinox_body": "Octarinox (შპს ოქტარინოქსი) is a small independent software studio in Tbilisi, Georgia, building open-source AI infrastructure for the rest of us. The name is a portmanteau — Octar from the eight directions of a compass, -inox from stainless: tools that point everywhere and don't rust. Our brand carries a Viking-Georgian sensibility because both cultures share a stubborn affection for craft, hospitality, and showing up to the workshop on Monday morning even when nobody's watching. We design tools we use ourselves, then release them so the community can use them too. If you find a bug, file an issue. If you find a feature missing, send a PR. If you find a typo in this paragraph, you have already proven you read it — congratulations.",
  "about.tech_title": "Built With",
  "about.tech_body": "PyQt6  ·  Groq  ·  OpenAI  ·  Anthropic  ·  Google Gemini  ·  Mistral AI  ·  keyring  ·  approximately 40,000 cups of espresso  ·  the patient encouragement of friends who said \"that's actually kind of cool\"",
  "about.license_title": "License",
  "about.license_body": "Released under the MIT License. Free for personal and commercial use, no strings attached. The license itself includes one small ceremonial clause for cultural sustenance — see LICENSE for details. (Non-binding. Definitely non-binding.)",
  "about.contribute_title": "Contributing",
  "about.contribute_body": "Pull requests, issues, feature ideas, polite criticism, impolite criticism (we'll forgive it), translations into your language, screenshots that make us look good, bug reports that make us look bad — all welcome. Visit the repository on GitHub. Stars are appreciated. Issues are appreciated more.",
  "about.thanks_title": "Acknowledgments",
  "about.thanks_body": "Thanks to the Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Mistral, and Groq teams for shipping the models that make this possible. Thanks to the PyQt and Riverbank Computing folks for the framework. Thanks to every developer who has ever opened an issue on a project they didn't have to. And thanks to you, for downloading this and giving it a chance.",
  "about.visit_github": "Visit GitHub",
  "about.report_issue": "Report Issue",
  "about.footer_motto": "Made with care, shared with love.",

